  "final_answer": "Based on the population pyramid of Japan in 2026 shown on the ingldata.com/jp/ interactive chart (which is the source data for the image in the English Wikipedia article 'Demographics of Japan'), the percentage of the total population that are **females aged 75-79 is 3.9%**.\n\nHere's how I determined this:\n\nThe SVG data extracted from the 2026 population pyramid shows age groups (100+, 95-99, 90-94, 85-89, 80-84, 75-79, 70-74, ...) with corresponding percentages for Males first, then Females:\n\n**Male percentages** (100+ to 0-4):\n0.0%, 0.1%, 0.6%, 1.3%, 2.1%, 3.3%, 2.9%, 2.9%, 3.2%, 3.7%, 4.0%, 3.3%, 2.9%, 2.6%, 2.5%, 2.6%, 2.6%, 2.4%, 2.2%, 1.9%, 1.6%\n\n**Female percentages** (100+ to 0-4):\n0.1%, 0.4%, 1.3%, 2.2%, 2.8%, **3.9%**, 3.2%, 3.0%, 3.1%, 3.6%, 4.0%, 3.3%, 2.9%, 2.5%, 2.4%, 2.5%, 2.5%, 2.2%, 2.1%, 1.8%, 1.5%\n\nThe 6th value in the Female series corresponds to the age group **75-79**, which is **3.9%** of the total population.\n\n(Total population in 2026: 122,427,743)",
